// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// T-1703 · Steam content-builder APP script for the RIMWARD DEMO.
//
// Driven by:  steamcmd +login <user> +run_app_build <abs path>/app_build_demo.vdf +quit
//
// THE IDS ARE PLACEHOLDERS ("0"), AND THAT IS DELIBERATE, NOT UNFINISHED.
// This repository holds no partner app id — packages/desktop/src/steam.ts's
// COMPILED_STEAM_APP_ID is null for exactly the same reason, and a unit test pins
// it so an id cannot be committed by accident. A committed real id would make
// every dev build talk to a live Steam product. Obtaining the demo app id and its
// depot id is part of setting up the store page (T-1704); filling them in is a
// two-line edit, here and in the depot script.
//
// A DEMO IS ITS OWN STEAM APP with its own depot — not a branch or a beta of the
// full app — which is why this is a second pair of scripts rather than a flag on
// a first pair. It matches the packaging split exactly: distinct appId, distinct
// productName, distinct output tree (electron-builder.demo.json).
//
// FORWARD SLASHES, deliberately: steamcmd accepts them on every platform, while a
// Windows-style path in a committed script breaks the moment the build runs on
// the macOS runner. Same rule scripts/copy-renderer.mjs follows.
//
// ContentRoot points at the UNPACKED tree, because that is what a Steam depot
// stores — Steam is the installer, so the NSIS .exe is for direct distribution
// only. The <200MB budget in src/size.ts measures that DISTRIBUTABLE artifact,
// for the reason given at its definition site.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
"appbuild"
{
	"appid"		"0"
	"desc"		"Rimward Demo - Tour One"
	"buildoutput"	"../release-demo/steam-build"
	"contentroot"	"../release-demo/win-unpacked"
	"setlive"	""

	"depots"
	{
		"0"	"depot_build_demo.vdf"
	}
}
